    "text_delta": "on will not meet the standard required for an internal grievance, ombudsman review, or human rights complaint.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Follow Up Professionally for Feedback:**  \n   Send a polite, forward-looking follow-up focused on career growth rather than grievance:\n   > *\"Thank you again for the opportunity to interview for the Director of Planning position. I understand your team is busy, but as I continue to pursue leadership roles, I would greatly appreciate 10–15 minutes of feedback on how I can strengthen my candidacy for similar opportunities in the future.\"*\n\n2. **Inquire About Specific Competencies:**  \n   If you secure a call, ask what competencies gave the successful candidate the advantage (e.g., council relations, community outreach, departmental leadership) so you can address any perceived gaps.\n\n3. **Check Hiring Transparency Policies (If Genuine Procedural Concerns Arise):**  \n   If you have concrete reasons to suspect procedural irregularity (e.g., scoring rules were violated or mandatory qualifications in the job posting were waived), municipal hiring policies and public records/freedom-of-information processes exist. However, pursue this only if there are documented administrative irregularities, not because of panel demographics.\n",
